你才不会把它送人呢。

318
00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.280
I wouldn't give that away.
我才不会送人。

319
00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.720
I would have bought it for someone else, but then kept it for myself.
我本来会买来送人，但最后肯定会留给自己。

320
00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:21.360
Well, Meredith is bummed that Pam only brought candy.
好吧，梅雷迪斯因为帕姆只带了糖果而感到沮丧。

321
00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:26.000
She's probably going to be even more bummed that it's going to take a while for Pam to set it out, but we'll get there.
她可能会因为帕姆还要过一会儿才拿出来而更加沮丧，但我们稍后会讲到。

322
00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.260
Yeah, what's up with that?
是啊，那到底是怎么回事？

323
00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:34.000
With the permission and the asking Michael, I was like, what is this weird power play happening over the candy?
关于许可和询问迈克尔那段，我当时就在想，这糖果背后到底在搞什么奇怪的权力博弈？

324
00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:35.860
I don't know, but I thought it was so funny.
我不知道，但我当时觉得太搞笑了。

325
00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:43.020
Well, now the episode's going to start, and Dwight is, um, well, he's starting his espionage.
好了，现在剧集要开始了，德怀特，嗯，他开始了他的间谍活动。

326
00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:47.480
Yeah, he storms into Jim's office, and he's like, two things.
没错，他冲进吉姆的办公室，说有两件事。

327
00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.020
Number one, stop leaving your pens on my desk.
第一，别再把你的笔留在我的桌子上了。

328
00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.500
Just because you got a promotion doesn't mean you get to leave your stuff all over the place.
别以为你升职了，就可以把东西到处乱放。

329
00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.480
And number two, congratulations on your promotion.
第二，祝贺你升职。

330
00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:05.740
And he does this, like, turn, and he's going to present him with a promotion gift of a wooden mallard.
然后他转了个身，准备送他一个升职礼物——一只木制野鸭。

331
00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:10.280
Well, Jim is going to say, thanks for the duck, and Dwight quickly says, mallard.
吉姆说，谢谢你的鸭子，德怀特立刻纠正说，是野鸭。

332
00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:14.680
He corrects people multiple times in this episode when they say duck.
这一集里他多次纠正别人说鸭子。

333
00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.520
He says mallard.
他说的是野鸭。

334
00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.820
So, Jenna, I had to know, what's the difference between a duck and a mallard?
所以，珍娜，我必须得问问，鸭子和野鸭到底有什么区别？

335
00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:22.340
Well, a mallard has a green head, and it's a male duck.
嗯，野鸭有绿色的头，是雄性鸭子。

336
00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:26.400
I know that from my summers at Lake of the Ozarks.
这是我在欧扎克湖度夏时学到的。

337
00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.940
We had lots of ducks.
我们那里有很多鸭子。

338
00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.280
Here's what the internet says.
互联网上是这么说的。

339
00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:31.000
Okay.
好的。

340
00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:34.000
There are over 120 species of ducks.
鸭子有超过120个品种。

341
00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.800
A mallard is just one type of duck.
野鸭只是鸭子的一种。

342
00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:42.640
Mallards are probably the most popular species of duck in North America, in Eurasian, wetlands,
野鸭可能是北美、欧亚大陆的湿地、

343
00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.680
parks, and ponds.
公园和池塘里最受欢迎的鸭子品种。

344
00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:47.060
This is a sexually dimorphic species of duck.
这是一种具有两性异形的鸭子。

345
00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.320
That means that the males and females look different from one another.
这意味着雄性和雌性长得不一样。

346
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.500
Male mallards sport bright green heads and are easily identified.
雄性野鸭有着鲜艳的绿色头部，很容易辨认。

347
00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:59.340
But female mallards are a brown color, not without their own subtle beauty.
但雌性野鸭是棕色的，也有一种微妙的美感。

348
00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.140
Both males and females have a blue patch in their wing.
雄性和雌性的翅膀上都有一个蓝色的斑块。

349
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:08.380
Mallards make the popular quack sound that most people associate to the sound of a duck.
野鸭会发出大多数人认为的鸭子那种标志性的嘎嘎声。

350
00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.620
And then it ended with this.
然后就以这个结束了。

351
00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:14.220
And a female mallard is particularly vocal.
而且雌性绿头鸭叫声特别响。

352
00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:17.280
Oh, there you go.
噢，原来如此。

353
00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:19.700
That's what the internet had to say about mallards.
这就是网上关于绿头鸭的内容。

354
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.800
We had mallards at my parents' lake house.
我父母的湖边小屋那边就有绿头鸭。

355
00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.160
We loved them.
我们很喜欢它们。

356
00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.480
Well, I'm not done.
好吧，我还没说完呢。

357
00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:29.400
Oh.
噢。

358
00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:30.940
Get ready for this.
准备好听这个。

359
00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:37.120
While Googling mallards, guess what was the first thing that came up, which was crazy to me.
我搜绿头鸭的时候，你猜第一个跳出来的是什么，我觉得简直不可思议。

360
00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:38.040
What?
什么？

361
00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.220
And I know you're going to think this is me having a thing for trains.
我知道你肯定会觉得我又在执着于火车了。

362
00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:51.840
But on July 3rd, 1938, a steam locomotive called the Mallard claimed the world speed record at 126 miles per hour.
但在1938年7月3日，一辆名为“绿头鸭号”的蒸汽机车以每小时126英里的速度创下了世界纪录。

363
00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:53.420
Oh.
噢。

364
00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:58.100
I think Google gave you that fact because it knows how much you like trains.
我觉得谷歌给你推送这个是因为它知道你有多喜欢火车。

365
00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.120
I guess it does.
我想确实是这样。

366
00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:02.440
I bet if I Googled mallards, I would not get that.
我敢打赌如果我搜绿头鸭，肯定不会搜到这个。

367
00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.740
I'm going to do it right now.
我现在就搜搜看。

368
00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:04.480
Okay.
好啊。

369
00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:05.020
I'm curious.
我很好奇。

370
00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:05.860
What did you Google?
你搜了什么？

371
00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:08.040
I Googled famous mallards.
我搜了“著名的绿头鸭”。

372
00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:10.800
Famous mallards.
著名的绿头鸭。

373
00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.280
I didn't know if there was like a popular story about a mallard.
我不知道有没有关于绿头鸭的流行故事。

374
00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:15.800
You know what comes up for me?
你知道我搜出来的是什么吗？

375
00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:16.460
What?
什么？

376
00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:20.220
A Wikipedia page called List of Fictional Ducks.
一个叫“虚构鸭子列表”的维基百科页面。

377
00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.200
Ah.
啊。

378
00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:23.760
Well, for me, this came up.
好吧，我这边搜出来的是这个。

379
00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:28.880
It was named the Mallard because Sir Herbert Nigel Gresley, hope I'm saying that right,
它之所以被命名为“绿头鸭号”，是因为赫伯特·奈杰尔·格雷斯利爵士——希望我没念错——

380
00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:36.580
was a British railway engineer who enjoyed breeding waterfowl as much as he loved making trains, I guess.
他是一位英国铁路工程师，我猜他喜欢养水禽就像他热爱制造火车一样。

381
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.520
He also designed a train he called the Flying Scotsman.
他还设计了一辆名为“飞行的苏格兰人号”的火车。

382
00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:49.900
And here's this, the A4 number 4468 Mallard still holds the record for being the fastest steam locomotive in the world.
还有这个，A4型4468号“绿头鸭”至今仍保持着世界上最快蒸汽机车的纪录。

383
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.780
I'm going to get you a train.
我要送你一辆火车。

384
00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:59.720
I was looking up information about mallards and I found a train.
我本来是在查绿头鸭的信息，结果却找到了一辆火车。

385
00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:04.260
I think it's an algorithm in your computer now.
我觉得你电脑里现在有某种算法了。

386
00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:07.360
It knows to show you these types of facts.
它知道该给你展示这类事实。

387
00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.720
I think you're going to get a lot of train facts.
我觉得你以后会收到很多关于火车的事实。

388
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.500
I also got some wallpaper with ducks on it.
我还搜到了一些印有鸭子的壁纸。

389
00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.100
You bought wallpaper with ducks?
你买了印有鸭子的壁纸？

390
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.520
No, wallpaper came up in my search.
没有，是搜索结果里出现了壁纸。

391
00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.540
If that tells you the other thing I've been Googling.
如果这能说明我最近还在搜些什么的话。

392
00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:21.980
Guys, I want a wallpaper.
伙计们，我想换个壁纸。

393
00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.160
Listen, that's a subject for later.
听着，那是以后再讨论的话题。

394
00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.620
Can I have duck wallpaper?
我可以换鸭子壁纸吗？

395
00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:26.920
Or train wallpaper?
或者火车壁纸？

396
00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.740
Or both duck and train wallpaper?
还是说鸭子和火车壁纸都要？

397
00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:29.840
Okay, I'm going to stop talking.
好吧，我不说了。

398
00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:32.280
I have an observation from this scene.
我对这一幕有个观察。

399
00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:33.200
What?
什么？

400
00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:40.580
So, remember last week when we were talking about the storyline of Aaron destroying Pam's watercolor?
还记得上周我们讨论亚伦毁掉帕姆水彩画的情节吗？

401
00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:41.640
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

402
00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:48.360
Well, at 1 minute 59 seconds, over Dwight's shoulder, he's standing in Jim's office,
嗯，在1分59秒的时候，越过德怀特的肩膀，他正站在吉姆的办公室里，

403
00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:54.380
you can see that there is nothing on the wall where Pam's watercolor should be.
你可以看到墙上原本应该挂着帕姆水彩画的地方什么都没有。

404
00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.440
And that is how it's going to be in this episode.
这一集里情况就是这样。

405
00:20:57.720 --> 00:20:59.020
The wall will be blank.
那面墙会是空的。

406
00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:04.760
There's another great shot of it at 4 minutes 53 seconds when Michael walks up to reception.
在4分53秒，当迈克尔走到前台时，有一个很棒的镜头拍到了那里。

407
00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:09.000
But next week, there's going to be something there.
但下周，那里就会有东西了。

408
00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:12.600
Not Pam's watercolor, but I'll point it out.
不是帕姆的水彩画，但我会指出来的。

409
00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:13.300
Okay.
好的。

410
00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:17.220
So, listen, ultimately Jim is going to take the duck.
所以，听着，最终吉姆会拿走那只鸭子。

411
00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.100
Dwight leaves.
德怀特离开了。

412
00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:24.440
He has a talking head where he reveals he inserted a listening device into the belly of the duck.
他有一个单人访谈，透露他在鸭子肚子里装了一个窃听装置。

413
00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.500
It looks like a walkie-talkie.
看起来像个对讲机。

414
00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:27.560
It is.
确实是。

415
00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:28.880
He calls it a listening device.
他管它叫窃听装置。

416
00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:33.360
This is a very crude system he's created.
这是他搞出来的一个非常简陋的系统。

417
00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:34.880
We'll find out why.
我们稍后会知道原因。

418
00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:35.800
Exactly.
没错。

419
00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:41.820
So, something I want to point out, as Jim is sitting at his desk and he puts the mallard down,
所以，我想指出一点，当吉姆坐在办公桌前放下那只野鸭时，

420
00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:47.380
at 2 minutes 50 seconds, there is a photo on Jim's desk of Pam.
在2分50秒，吉姆的桌上有一张帕姆的照片。

421
00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:50.180
Do you know what the photo is?
你知道那是什么照片吗？

422
00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:51.100
No.
不知道。

423
00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:57.420
It is that old, fuzzy-haired photo of Pam with her eyes half-closed.
就是那张帕姆头发毛茸茸的、眼睛半闭的老照片。

424
00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.840
It's the one they put the beans on.
就是他们往上面放豆子的那张。

425
00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.500
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

426
00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:07.140
Why has he framed this weird picture of Pam and put it on his desk?
他为什么要把这张奇怪的帕姆照片装裱起来放在桌上？

427
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:08.840
It was so weird to me.
我觉得太奇怪了。

428
00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.780
It's weird.
确实很怪。

429
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:11.820
I don't know.
我不知道。

430
00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:16.800
I don't know what that was about, but I'm going to track it because it's suddenly on his desk,
我不知道那是怎么回事，但我会追踪这件事，因为它突然出现在他桌上，

431
00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.240
and I'm curious, is it going to stay there?
我很好奇，它会一直放在那儿吗？

432
00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:22.140
How long will the fuzzy picture of Pam be on the desk?
那张毛茸茸的帕姆照片会在桌上放多久？

433
00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:23.220
Tracking it.
追踪它。

434
00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:24.260
Tracking it.
追踪它。

435
00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:29.160
We have a delicious Jim and Michael scene coming up in the kitchen.
接下来我们在厨房有一场吉姆和迈克尔的精彩对手戏。

436
00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:34.800
Jenna, I just feel like you know you're in for a doozy of a conversation.
珍娜，我总觉得你知道接下来要面对一场重头戏了。

437
00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.780
If it starts with, I have recently taken a lover.
如果对话是以“我最近有了个情人”开头的。

438
00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:43.560
I mean, if you're leading in with that line, I'm going to get a cup of tea and sit down.
我是说，如果对方用这句话开场，我肯定会去泡杯茶坐下来。

439
00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:44.440
I'm going to get comfortable.
我要找个舒服的姿势。

440
00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:47.380
You know, Jim says, who's the lucky lady?
你知道，吉姆问，哪位幸运女士？

441
00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:50.480
John is totally breaking when he says that.
约翰说这句话的时候完全笑场了。

442
00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:51.560
Did you see?
你看到了吗？

443
00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:53.680
He's like, who's the lucky lady?
他就像是说，哪位幸运女士？

444
00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:55.780
Like, that is John right there.
那简直就是约翰本人。

445
00:22:56.740 --> 00:23:01.900
And then I laughed so hard when Jim's like, you did not have sex with Pam's mom.
然后当吉姆说“你没跟帕姆的妈妈发生关系吧”时，我笑得不行。

446
00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:03.220
And Michael's like, oh, big time.
迈克尔回答说，噢，那必须的。

447
00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:04.920
And Jim says, what kind of car does she drive?
吉姆问，她开什么车？

448
00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:07.280
And Michael goes, a green Camry.
迈克尔说，一辆绿色凯美瑞。

449
00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.300
And Jim's like, s***.
吉姆说，该死。

450
00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.880
Oh, yeah, that was not in the script.
噢，没错，那句台词剧本里没有。

451
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.740
That curse, that was on the day.
那个诅咒，就在那天发生了。

452
00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:14.300
Yeah.
是啊。

453
00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:18.460
And then just everything about the beats of the scene is so funny.
而且这一幕的节奏处理得太搞笑了。

454
00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:21.280
And when Jim is like, find a new way home, man.
还有吉姆说的那句，换条路回家吧，伙计。

455
00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:25.760
Oh, we got a fan question about that from Jessica S.
哦，我们收到一个来自南卡罗来纳州哥伦比亚市的杰西卡·S的粉丝提问。

456
00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:27.320
in Columbia, South Carolina.
关于那个问题的。

457
00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:30.900
She said, in season two, episode two,
她说，在第二季第二集里，

458
00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:33.860
Pam says that her mom lives about two hours away.
帕姆说她妈妈住在离这儿大约两小时车程的地方。

459
00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:40.220
But in this episode, Michael says it's easy to date Pam's mom because she's on his way home from work.
但这一集里，迈克尔说和帕姆的妈妈约会很方便，因为她就在他下班回家的路上。

460
00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:42.340
Did Pam's mom move?
帕姆的妈妈搬家了吗？

461
00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:44.060
Yes.
是的。

462
