783
00:38:17.830 --> 00:38:19.970
She needs him to be more upset about this.
她需要他为此感到更难过。

784
00:38:20.210 --> 00:38:21.850
This is his mother now, too.
现在这也是他妈了。

785
00:38:22.550 --> 00:38:25.390
She says, your mother is sleeping with Michael Scott.
她说，你妈在跟迈克尔·斯科特睡觉。

786
00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:26.710
Oh.
噢。

787
00:38:27.350 --> 00:38:27.790
Yeah.
是啊。

788
00:38:27.850 --> 00:38:30.530
And then she just walks away and lets him sit in that moment.
然后她就走开了，让他独自消化那一刻。

789
00:38:31.570 --> 00:38:34.190
And with that, I think we should take a break.
说到这，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

790
00:38:34.790 --> 00:38:38.790
But I want to point out, I have still not revealed what's on my two cards.
但我得指出，我还没揭晓我那两张卡片上写了什么。

791
00:38:39.470 --> 00:38:39.910
Yeah.
是啊。

792
00:38:40.010 --> 00:38:40.870
Will you get to it?
你会揭晓吗？

793
00:38:40.930 --> 00:38:41.710
I'm so curious.
我太好奇了。

794
00:38:42.070 --> 00:38:42.910
I'll get to it.
我会揭晓的。

795
00:38:43.150 --> 00:38:44.570
It'll be in this next part.
就在下一部分。

796
00:38:44.790 --> 00:38:45.590
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

797
00:38:45.590 --> 00:38:55.960
We are back.
我们回来了。

798
00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:59.820
And Jenna, spill the beans on the green card and the blue card.
珍娜，快揭晓绿卡和蓝卡上的秘密吧。

799
00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:02.540
Well, the blue card is first up, Angela.
好吧，先从蓝卡开始，安吉拉。

800
00:39:02.820 --> 00:39:05.740
We're in the scene where Jim asks Andy to come in his office.
我们现在拍的是吉姆叫安迪进他办公室的那场戏。

801
00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:08.820
He's going to start blasting some opera music.
他准备开始播放歌剧音乐了。

802
00:39:09.460 --> 00:39:12.380
And of course, this is driving Dwight crazy.
当然，这让德怀特快疯了。

803
00:39:12.380 --> 00:39:20.980
The aria that Jim is playing is from a German opera called Martha by Friedrich von Floteau.
吉姆放的那段咏叹调出自弗里德里希·冯·弗洛托创作的德国歌剧《玛莎》。

804
00:39:21.540 --> 00:39:24.200
It is a romantic comedy opera lady.
那是一部浪漫喜剧歌剧，女士。

805
00:39:24.620 --> 00:39:26.320
Everyone in the office is hearing it.
办公室里的每个人都听到了。

806
00:39:26.500 --> 00:39:28.840
And Creed starts crying.
克里德开始哭了起来。

807
00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:35.040
Oh, I had so many background catches as we went around the room.
哦，我们在环顾房间时，我捕捉到了好多背景细节。

808
00:39:35.040 --> 00:39:41.480
At 9 minutes, 40 seconds, the camera zooms in on you, Angela, listening to the opera.
在9分40秒时，镜头推向了正在听歌剧的你，安吉拉。

809
00:39:41.760 --> 00:39:45.820
And the whiteboard over your shoulder says this.
你肩膀上方的白板上写着这个。

810
00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:46.820
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

811
00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:51.240
It says, Post-it Rep Joe, 4 p.m.
上面写着：便利贴代表乔，下午4点。

812
00:39:51.300 --> 00:39:52.000
with Phyllis.
和菲利斯一起。

813
00:39:53.240 --> 00:39:57.000
A Post-it Rep is coming in to talk to Phyllis, Angela.
安吉拉，有个便利贴公司的代表要来找菲利斯谈话。

814
00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:04.000
And then at 9 minutes, 45 seconds, when the camera shows that Creed is crying,
然后在9分45秒，当镜头拍到克里德在哭的时候，

815
00:40:04.860 --> 00:40:09.380
I noticed that Creed has a photo of himself taped to the wall.
我注意到克里德在墙上贴了一张他自己的照片。

816
00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:12.140
A headshot of himself.
一张他自己的头像照。

817
00:40:12.520 --> 00:40:15.180
Not even in a frame, just taped to the wall.
甚至都没装框，就直接贴在墙上。

818
00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:16.340
Just taped to the wall.
就直接贴在墙上。

819
00:40:16.700 --> 00:40:17.220
Freestyle.
随性而为。

820
00:40:17.520 --> 00:40:18.000
That tracks.
这很符合他的风格。

821
00:40:18.740 --> 00:40:20.500
But here's what I'm going to tell you.
但我要告诉你这个。

822
00:40:20.600 --> 00:40:23.640
Here's the late breaking info that came in from Randy Cordray.
这是兰迪·科德雷刚发来的最新消息。

823
00:40:23.820 --> 00:40:26.640
It's about that song that Jim is playing.
是关于吉姆放的那首歌的。

824
00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:30.680
He said that that song was public domain.
他说那首歌属于公共领域。

825
00:40:31.260 --> 00:40:37.940
However, we had to pay $1,500 in royalty rights to play that particular recording.
然而，我们为了播放那个特定的录音版本，不得不支付了1500美元的版权费。

826
00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:40.340
Stuff you don't think about.
这些是你平时不会去想的事情。

827
00:40:40.740 --> 00:40:42.920
Stuff I don't think about when I watch a show.
也是我平时看剧时不会去想的事情。

828
00:40:43.200 --> 00:40:43.580
Nope.
没错。

829
00:40:43.760 --> 00:40:44.980
I do now, though.
不过我现在会想了。

830
00:40:45.760 --> 00:40:48.620
Well, now Michael is going to hold a meeting in the conference room.
好了，现在迈克尔要在会议室开会了。

831
00:40:48.820 --> 00:40:50.980
A lot happens in this meeting.
这次会议发生了很多事。

832
00:40:51.480 --> 00:40:55.800
And yet I titled this scene, Ryan Has a Hat.
但我给这一幕起的标题是：瑞安戴了顶帽子。

833
00:40:56.480 --> 00:40:57.220
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

834
00:40:57.660 --> 00:41:03.860
I wrote down, at 10 minutes, 35 seconds, we see Ryan's fedora for the first time.
我记下了，在10分35秒时，我们第一次看到了瑞安的软呢帽。

835
00:41:04.200 --> 00:41:05.220
Out of the blue.
突如其来。

836
00:41:05.420 --> 00:41:06.320
No explanation.
没有任何解释。

837
00:41:06.720 --> 00:41:06.770
Out of the blue.
突如其来。

838
00:41:06.780 --> 00:41:07.860
What's going on?
到底怎么回事？

839
00:41:07.860 --> 00:41:13.540
This conference room meeting is actually going to be about the fact that corporate wants
这次会议实际上是关于公司希望

840
00:41:13.540 --> 00:41:18.500
each branch to brainstorm ways to better communicate with their community.
每个分部集思广益，想出如何更好地与社区沟通的方法。

841
00:41:19.340 --> 00:41:25.680
And whoever comes up with the best idea is going to get a $50 gift certificate to a local restaurant.
谁能想出最好的点子，就能获得一张价值50美元的当地餐厅礼券。

842
00:41:26.040 --> 00:41:32.720
I want to point out, when Jim announces the $50 gift certificate, how happy everyone was.
我想指出的是，当吉姆宣布那张50美元的礼券时，大家有多高兴。

843
00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:38.160
There's a reaction shot pass, and we're all like, even Angela Martin is like, oh, that's nice.
镜头扫过大家的反应，我们都觉得，连安吉拉·马丁都觉得，哦，那挺好的。

844
00:41:38.600 --> 00:41:39.540
Good incentive.
不错的激励措施。

845
00:41:39.900 --> 00:41:40.920
Everyone likes food.
大家都喜欢食物。

846
00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:49.560
People are shouting out ideas, but Pam is going to suggest that Michael leaving Scranton would make Scranton a better place.
大家都在大声提建议，但帕姆却暗示迈克尔离开斯克兰顿会让斯克兰顿变得更好。

847
00:41:49.780 --> 00:41:51.360
That would help the community.
那会对社区有帮助。

848
00:41:51.820 --> 00:41:53.440
Oh, Pam's turning up the heat.
哦，帕姆开始施压了。

849
00:41:53.720 --> 00:42:01.760
She literally starts chanting, no more meetings, and stands up, like waving her hands about, no more meetings.
她甚至开始高喊“不要再开会了”，还站起来挥舞着双手，喊着“不要再开会了”。

850
00:42:01.760 --> 00:42:05.080
Yes, we had a fan question from Zach M.
是的，我们收到了扎克·M发来的粉丝提问。

851
00:42:05.280 --> 00:42:07.160
in Venice Center, New York.
在纽约的威尼斯中心。

852
00:42:07.520 --> 00:42:14.540
In the conference room scene, was it Leslie David Baker's idea to join in with Pam's no more meetings?
在会议室的那场戏里，莱斯利·大卫·贝克加入帕姆的“不再开会”行列，那是他的主意吗？

853
00:42:15.380 --> 00:42:17.260
Or was that in the script?
还是剧本里本来就有的？

854
00:42:18.320 --> 00:42:22.160
I also just love his reaction when Michael says, I'm sensual.
我也特别喜欢迈克尔说“我很性感”时他的反应。

855
00:42:22.540 --> 00:42:23.040
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

856
00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:25.660
Stanley is the king of facial sass.
斯坦利简直是“表情嘲讽”之王。

857
00:42:25.840 --> 00:42:28.020
I loved the term facial sass.
我很喜欢“表情嘲讽”这个词。

858
00:42:28.260 --> 00:42:28.920
Yeah, me too.
我也是。

859
00:42:29.820 --> 00:42:30.920
You know what?
你知道吗？

860
00:42:31.160 --> 00:42:33.260
Guys, that was all Leslie.
伙计们，那全是莱斯利自己发挥的。

861
00:42:33.500 --> 00:42:42.480
It was not scripted that anyone should join in with Pam, but he made the choice to be delighted, and I absolutely love it.
剧本里并没有写要有人加入帕姆，但他选择了表现出那种欣喜，我真的太喜欢了。

862
00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:51.420
During Pam's rally cry to get meetings canceled, Michael gets a phone call, and he starts to take it.
在帕姆呼吁取消会议时，迈克尔接到了一个电话，他开始接听。

863
00:42:51.820 --> 00:42:58.360
This was the moment my character decides to raise her hand and participate, and Jim's like, yes, Angela,
那一刻，我的角色决定举手参与，吉姆说，好的，安吉拉，

864
00:42:58.360 --> 00:42:59.840
you should tell us your ideas.
你应该告诉我们你的想法。

865
00:43:00.280 --> 00:43:06.920
And I go off into my speech about the accounting department, and the rest of the room, they don't give a crap about what Angela's saying.
于是我开始发表关于会计部门的演讲，而房间里的其他人，根本不在乎安吉拉在说什么。

866
00:43:07.060 --> 00:43:12.500
They want to hear Michael's phone call because he starts it off, and he's saying, no, no one talks to my baby that way.
他们想听迈克尔的电话，因为他一开口就说，不，没人能那样跟我宝贝说话。

867
00:43:13.260 --> 00:43:14.780
Yeah, yeah, no, I'll talk to her.
对，对，不，我会跟她说的。

868
00:43:15.160 --> 00:43:16.900
This is all anyone wants to hear.
这才是大家想听的内容。

869
00:43:17.700 --> 00:43:18.500
For sure.
确实。

870
00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:25.440
It was really hard for me to do those lines so seriously because we were all cracking up.
我很难那么严肃地念出那些台词，因为我们当时都快笑场了。

871
00:43:26.140 --> 00:43:29.740
Steve was being so funny, and I checked the script.
史蒂夫当时太搞笑了，我查了剧本。

872
00:43:30.040 --> 00:43:32.920
Everything he's saying was totally scripted.
他说的每一句话都是剧本里写好的。

873
00:43:33.080 --> 00:43:34.020
All of that.
全部都是。

874
00:43:34.120 --> 00:43:34.760
It was perfect.
太完美了。

875
00:43:35.080 --> 00:43:35.760
It was perfect.
太完美了。

876
00:43:35.760 --> 00:43:45.260
The only line that I caught that was improvised was actually by Brian Baumgartner because when Michael comes back in the room, Kevin says, who's Pickle?
我发现唯一即兴发挥的台词其实是布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳说的，因为当迈克尔回到房间时，凯文说，“皮克尔是谁？”

877
00:43:45.800 --> 00:43:46.300
Yes.
没错。

878
00:43:46.740 --> 00:43:48.060
And that was not in the script.
那句台词剧本里没有。

879
00:43:48.320 --> 00:43:50.340
Yes, and that made us laugh, too.
是的，那也把我们逗笑了。

880
00:43:51.380 --> 00:43:54.280
I don't know if you noticed when Michael's phone rang.
不知道你们有没有注意到迈克尔电话响的时候。

881
00:43:54.380 --> 00:43:56.560
It had a distinct ringtone.
那铃声很特别。

882
00:43:56.920 --> 00:43:59.080
I couldn't put my finger on it, though.
但我当时没听出来是什么。

883
00:43:59.540 --> 00:44:00.580
Did you pick it up?
你听出来了吗？

884
00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:02.460
I played it over and over and over again.
我反复听了好多次。

885
00:44:03.060 --> 00:44:06.540
I just noticed that it wasn't like a standard ringtone.
我只是注意到那不是普通的铃声。

886
00:44:07.220 --> 00:44:12.260
And Michael is known for having special songs on his phone.
迈克尔手机里总是有一些特别的歌曲。

887
00:44:12.260 --> 00:44:16.720
Right, so maybe this ringtone was assigned to Pam's mom for a reason.
对，所以也许这个铃声是专门为帕姆的妈妈设置的。

888
00:44:17.100 --> 00:44:26.740
I couldn't figure it out, but in the script, it says that Michael's cell phone ring is supposed to be the song Sexual Healing.
我没听出来，但剧本里写着迈克尔的手机铃声应该是《Sexual Healing》这首歌。

889
00:44:27.740 --> 00:44:30.120
This brings me back to the blue card.
这让我想起了那张蓝卡。

890
00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:36.540
Sure enough, we did pay to have his ringtone be Sexual Healing.
果然，我们确实付钱买了《Sexual Healing》作为他的铃声。

891
00:44:36.540 --> 00:44:38.020
That is what is playing.
那就是当时播放的音乐。

892
00:44:38.020 --> 00:44:44.120
We paid $26,500 just for that ringtone.
我们光为了那个铃声就付了26500美元。

893
00:44:44.780 --> 00:44:49.060
Which I'm sad to say, the joke didn't even land when I heard it.
很遗憾地说，我听到的时候，那个笑话甚至没能产生效果。

894
00:44:49.480 --> 00:44:50.940
Someone must have caught it.
肯定有人注意到了。

895
00:44:51.220 --> 00:44:53.360
Out there in the world, someone caught it.
在世界上的某个地方，肯定有人注意到了。

896
00:44:53.580 --> 00:44:58.140
But yeah, that ringtone also is only like six seconds.
不过确实，那个铃声也就只有六秒左右。

897
00:44:58.660 --> 00:45:00.160
If that, yes.
甚至可能更短，没错。

898
00:45:01.040 --> 00:45:04.880
Well, after Michael's phone call, everyone's going to learn that he's dating Pam's mom.
好吧，在迈克尔接完电话后，大家都知道他在和帕姆的妈妈约会了。

899
00:45:05.060 --> 00:45:06.920
And they're like, Michael, you're out of line.
他们说，迈克尔，你太过分了。

900
00:45:07.220 --> 00:45:09.920
And then Michael makes this impassioned speech.
然后迈克尔发表了一段慷慨激昂的演讲。

901
00:45:10.100 --> 00:45:13.200
You know, like, why can't I have love, you know?
你知道，就是，为什么我就不能拥有爱情呢，你懂吗？

902
00:45:13.780 --> 00:45:14.180
Yeah.
是啊。

903
00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:17.180
And then Phyllis is like, well, Michael, I wish you luck.
然后菲利斯就说，好吧，迈克尔，祝你好运。

904
00:45:17.300 --> 00:45:18.960
And then Oscar starts to chime in.
接着奥斯卡开始插嘴。

905
00:45:19.080 --> 00:45:20.640
And Pam is like, shut up, Oscar.
帕姆就说，闭嘴，奥斯卡。

906
00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:25.800
This really starts a battle between Michael and Pam.
这真的引发了迈克尔和帕姆之间的一场大战。

907
00:45:26.320 --> 00:45:31.840
Yeah, you know, everyone's on Pam's side, but they quickly turn to Michael's side.
是啊，你知道，起初大家都站在帕姆那边，但很快就倒戈向迈克尔了。

908
00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:34.020
And this is even more frustrating for Pam.
这对帕姆来说就更令人沮丧了。

909
00:45:34.360 --> 00:45:38.640
The news comes out, she thinks she's going to have backup, and she doesn't.
消息传开后，她本以为会有后援，结果并没有。

910
00:45:38.940 --> 00:45:43.220
I mean, even to the point where when she walks up to accounting,
我的意思是，甚至当她走到会计部时，

911
00:45:43.900 --> 00:45:47.240
Angela gives her a little sarcastic sass.
安吉拉还给了她一点讽刺的挖苦。

912
00:45:47.740 --> 00:45:48.920
Angela's enjoying this.
安吉拉很享受这一刻。

913
00:45:49.000 --> 00:45:49.480
Are you kidding?
你开玩笑吧？

914
00:45:49.480 --> 00:45:51.500
Angela's about to bust out some popcorn.
安吉拉都快要拿出爆米花来看戏了。

915
00:45:52.080 --> 00:45:56.140
Well, lady, we got fan mail from Jamie in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania,
好吧，女士，我们收到了来自宾夕法尼亚州匹兹堡的杰米的粉丝来信，

916
00:45:56.480 --> 00:46:00.280
who said, Angela, your delivery of Pam, how's your day going,
他说，安吉拉，你对帕姆说的那句“你今天过得怎么样”，

917
00:46:00.500 --> 00:46:04.720
is my all-time favorite line in the entire series.
是我整部剧里最喜欢的台词。

918
00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:05.360
What?
什么？

919
00:46:06.100 --> 00:46:09.420
It is absolutely perfect and hilarious.
那简直太完美、太搞笑了。

920
00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:11.540
Thank you.
谢谢你。

921
00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:16.680
Jamie, I think we might need to send you an Angela Sass sweatshirt.
杰米，我想我们可能得送你一件“安吉拉式挖苦”的卫衣。

922
00:46:16.900 --> 00:46:17.820
Oh, we should.
哦，我们应该送。

923
00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:20.860
You like yourself some Angela Sass.
你很喜欢安吉拉的挖苦风格嘛。

924
00:46:21.020 --> 00:46:23.480
We're going to figure out how to get that to you.
我们会想办法把它送到你手上的。

925
00:46:24.040 --> 00:46:25.020
Thank you, Jamie.
谢谢你，杰米。

926
00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:27.880
It was very fun to play something other than angry.
能演一些除了愤怒之外的情绪真的很有趣。

927
00:46:28.140 --> 00:46:31.740
And so being that, like, passive-aggressive bitch was delicious.
所以能演那种被动攻击的贱人感觉真是太爽了。

928
00:46:32.780 --> 00:46:35.580
Well, Pam and Michael have clearly drawn a line in the sand.
好吧，帕姆和迈克尔显然已经划清了界限。

929
00:46:35.800 --> 00:46:37.280
She wants him to leave the office.
她想让他离开办公室。

930
00:46:37.440 --> 00:46:38.820
He's like, I'm willing to die here.
他却说，我宁愿死在这里。

931
00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:40.500
She's like, I'm willing to die here.
她说，我也宁愿死在这里。

932
00:46:41.140 --> 00:46:42.760
And there's a standoff.
于是陷入了僵局。

933
00:46:43.080 --> 00:46:46.560
There was an amazing deleted runner between Michael and Jim,
迈克尔和吉姆之间有一段很棒的删减片段，

934
00:46:46.740 --> 00:46:52.080
where Michael is pleading to Jim to please help him with Pam.
迈克尔恳求吉姆帮他搞定帕姆。

935
00:46:52.300 --> 00:46:53.820
It starts in the kitchen.
是从厨房开始的。

936
00:46:54.120 --> 00:46:55.600
I want you to hear part of it.
我想让你们听听其中的一部分。

937
00:46:56.700 --> 00:46:59.700
I need you to side with me on this.
我需要你在这件事上支持我。

938
00:46:59.920 --> 00:47:01.060
You're the boss.
你是老板。

939
00:47:01.380 --> 00:47:03.920
Everybody here considers you to be the boss more than me.
这里每个人都觉得你比我更像老板。

940
00:47:04.020 --> 00:47:04.760
Well, that's crazy.
好吧，那太疯狂了。

941
00:47:04.900 --> 00:47:06.540
Because you've been the boss way longer.
因为你当老板的时间长多了。

942
00:47:06.540 --> 00:47:09.520
So you've dealt with situations just like this dozens of times.
所以你肯定处理过几十次像这样的情况了。

943
00:47:09.720 --> 00:47:12.340
I think that you can solve this.
我觉得你能解决这个问题。

944
00:47:12.480 --> 00:47:15.300
Because I am not that smart.
因为我没那么聪明。

945
00:47:15.840 --> 00:47:16.500
Toilet guard?
厕所守卫？

946
00:47:16.920 --> 00:47:17.740
Golden ticket?
黄金入场券？

947
00:47:18.020 --> 00:47:19.440
You're a creative mastermind.
你是个创意天才。

948
00:47:19.440 --> 00:47:21.580
You have a relationship with Pam.
你和帕姆有交情。

949
00:47:21.880 --> 00:47:23.540
You know her better than I do.
你比我更了解她。

950
00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:25.620
Michael, you know Pam way better than I do.
迈克尔，你比我更了解帕姆。

951
00:47:25.800 --> 00:47:28.060
That's only partially true.
那只说对了一部分。

952
00:47:29.860 --> 00:47:34.740
So then the scene somehow becomes this who's the best boss off.
所以场景不知怎么就变成了“谁才是最好的老板”的较量。

953
00:47:34.880 --> 00:47:38.080
Because whoever's the better boss is who has to go handle Pam.
因为谁是更好的老板，谁就得去应付帕姆。

954
00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:39.880
I am an idiot.
我真是个白痴。

955
00:47:40.200 --> 00:47:41.620
You're brilliant, man.
你太聪明了，伙计。

956
00:47:41.920 --> 00:47:45.060
You know I wouldn't even know where to start, Michael.
你知道我甚至都不知道该从哪儿下手，迈克尔。

957
00:47:45.060 --> 00:47:48.700
You are an excellent moderator, boss, friend.
你是一位出色的调解员、老板，也是朋友。

958
00:47:48.700 --> 00:47:51.680
You are the greatest sleight of hand magician I've ever seen.
你是我见过最厉害的魔术师。

959
00:47:51.820 --> 00:47:52.820
You're the man for the job.
你就是干这活儿的最佳人选。

960
00:47:53.120 --> 00:47:54.540
That's why you were promoted.
这就是你被提拔的原因。

961
00:47:54.800 --> 00:47:55.800
I can't lie anymore.
我没法再撒谎了。

962
00:47:55.800 --> 00:47:56.700
You're a genius.
你是天才。

963
00:47:56.980 --> 00:47:58.240
Well, okay.
好吧，行。

964
00:47:58.560 --> 00:47:59.280
All right.
没问题。

965
00:48:03.850 --> 00:48:05.510
That just made me laugh.
那刚才真把我逗乐了。

966
00:48:06.930 --> 00:48:10.630
I guess Michael's going to end up going to Toby.
我猜迈克尔最终还是得去找托比。

967
00:48:11.570 --> 00:48:14.210
Yeah, because he went to Jim and it didn't work.
没错，因为他找过吉姆，但没用。

968
00:48:14.290 --> 00:48:17.570
He won the best boss off and he doesn't want to deal with Pam.
他赢了“最佳老板”的较量，但他不想去应付帕姆。

969
00:48:17.570 --> 00:48:22.050
So he is now having to choose his last resort.
所以他现在不得不选择最后的一招。

970
00:48:22.430 --> 00:48:24.290
He gives Toby a hug.
他给了托比一个拥抱。

971
00:48:24.950 --> 00:48:29.090
There were so many moments in the scene that I thought were just perfection.
那一幕里有很多瞬间我觉得简直完美。

972
00:48:29.450 --> 00:48:34.630
First of all, when he goes to sit down and Toby's like, I can get you a chair or you can sit on the shredder.
首先，当他走过去坐下时，托比说：“我可以给你拿把椅子，或者你可以坐在碎纸机上。”

973
00:48:34.870 --> 00:48:35.130
Okay.
好吧。

974
00:48:35.670 --> 00:48:36.030
Yeah.
是啊。

975
00:48:36.870 --> 00:48:43.490
And also Toby's talking head where he is like, he always knew that he and Michael would become friends.
还有托比的采访镜头，他说他一直都知道自己和迈克尔会成为朋友。

976
00:48:43.810 --> 00:48:44.270
Yeah.
是啊。

977
00:48:44.350 --> 00:48:46.270
If Michael could just give him a chance, you know.
只要迈克尔能给他一个机会，你知道的。

978
00:48:46.670 --> 00:48:47.910
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

979
00:48:48.450 --> 00:48:49.010
Heartbreaking.
太令人心碎了。

980
00:48:49.930 --> 00:48:57.850
I also think that Toby is very excited to have a reason to go talk to Pam, but it does not go well.
我还觉得托比很兴奋能有个理由去和帕姆谈话，但结果并不顺利。

981
00:48:58.010 --> 00:48:58.550
No.
确实。

982
00:48:59.130 --> 00:48:59.750
At all.
一点也不顺利。

983
00:48:59.750 --> 00:49:02.110
And Michael immediately turns on Toby.
而且迈克尔立刻就翻脸不认人了。

984
00:49:02.570 --> 00:49:08.730
Oh, by the way, lady, we skipped over a very important scene over in Kelly's nook.
哦，顺便说一下，女士，我们跳过了一个在凯莉的小隔间里非常重要的场景。

985
00:49:09.070 --> 00:49:18.770
Yes, the fedora moment because Dwight is all of a sudden hearing a conversation between Kelly and Ryan through the mallard walkie-talkie.
没错，就是那个软呢帽的桥段，因为德怀特突然通过那个野鸭对讲机听到了凯莉和瑞安的谈话。

986
00:49:19.050 --> 00:49:22.250
We can hear Kelly talking about Ryan's fedora.
我们能听到凯莉在谈论瑞安的软呢帽。

987
00:49:22.450 --> 00:49:23.490
She wants to get one.
她想买一顶。

988
00:49:23.750 --> 00:49:25.070
Where did he get his?
他是在哪儿买的？

989
00:49:25.270 --> 00:49:25.990
She asks.
她问。

990
00:49:26.470 --> 00:49:28.010
He says, I'd rather not say.
他说，我不想说。

991
00:49:28.190 --> 00:49:29.530
Yeah, he doesn't want to get into it.
是啊，他不想深究这件事。

992
00:49:29.750 --> 00:49:30.170
No.
没错。

993
00:49:30.610 --> 00:49:37.910
All the while, Dwight is running back to Kelly's nook and sees the mallard on her desk.
与此同时，德怀特跑回凯莉的小隔间，看到了她桌上的野鸭。

994
00:49:38.830 --> 00:49:40.090
A gift from Jim.
那是吉姆送的礼物。

995
00:49:40.570 --> 00:49:44.270
And once again, Dwight is like, where did you get that mallard?
德怀特又一次问：“你从哪儿弄来的那只野鸭？”

996
00:49:44.370 --> 00:49:45.970
And Kelly's like, what the hell is a mallard?
凯莉说：“野鸭到底是什么鬼？”

997
00:49:46.110 --> 00:49:47.670
Oh, Professor Damian D.
哦，达米安·D教授。

998
00:49:47.870 --> 00:49:48.090
Duck?
鸭子？

999
00:49:49.210 --> 00:49:49.750
Yeah.
是啊。

1000
00:49:50.770 --> 00:49:55.310
I want to say that we got some fan mail from Kiri C.
我想说我们收到了一封来自Kiri C的粉丝来信。

1001
00:49:55.530 --> 00:50:01.970
in North Hollywood, California, who pointed out that Ryan is not wearing a fedora.
在加利福尼亚州北好莱坞，有人指出瑞安戴的不是软呢帽。

1002
00:50:01.970 --> 00:50:05.370
He is wearing a trilby.
他戴的是爵士帽。

1003
00:50:06.030 --> 00:50:08.490
It's a different kind of hat.
那是另一种帽子。

1004
00:50:09.070 --> 00:50:10.750
I looked this up.
我特意查过。

1005
00:50:10.970 --> 00:50:18.170
The main difference between these two hats, they're shaped very similarly, but it's the size of the brim.
这两种帽子外形很像，主要区别在于帽檐的大小。

1006
00:50:19.370 --> 00:50:26.170
Kiri noted that trilbys were very popular during this time, but they were often misidentified as fedoras.
基里提到，爵士帽在当时非常流行，但常被误认为是软呢帽。

1007
00:50:26.170 --> 00:50:37.730
Because this trend was often found with, quote, gents like Ryan, who had a tendency to condescendingly explain things to others.
因为这种潮流常出现在像瑞安这样的男士身上，他们往往喜欢居高临下地给别人科普。

1008
00:50:37.730 --> 00:50:50.530
Even though the information was not accurate, this moment just is so peak Ryan that Ryan would be walking around wearing a trilby but calling it a fedora.
尽管信息并不准确，但这一刻简直太“瑞安”了，瑞安戴着爵士帽却管它叫软呢帽，到处招摇。

1009
00:50:52.050 --> 00:50:57.610
I do vaguely remember that, like, I feel like Brad Pitt used to wear these or something.
我隐约记得，感觉布拉德·皮特以前好像戴过这种帽子。

1010
00:50:57.910 --> 00:51:01.410
Like, I feel like I remember seeing, like, big celebrities wearing these hats.
我好像记得看到过大明星戴这种帽子。

1011
00:51:01.730 --> 00:51:02.470
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1012
00:51:02.470 --> 00:51:05.130
It was like a mini moment.
那曾是一阵小小的风潮。

1013
00:51:05.130 --> 00:51:06.170
It was the moment.
那可是当时的风潮。

1014
00:51:06.170 --> 00:51:09.490
These trilby hats on the gents.
男士们戴的这种爵士帽。

1015
00:51:09.910 --> 00:51:11.510
The hipster gents.
那些文青男士。

1016
00:51:11.650 --> 00:51:12.410
The hipsters.
那些文青。

1017
00:51:13.230 --> 00:51:18.970
Lady, we're getting near the end of this episode, and I'd like to get out my green index card.
女士，这集快录完了，我想拿出我的绿色索引卡。

1018
00:51:19.230 --> 00:51:20.930
Oh, this is the personal stuff.
噢，这是要聊私事了。

1019
00:51:21.130 --> 00:51:22.290
This is personal.
这是私事。

1020
00:51:22.670 --> 00:51:25.390
Totally unrelated to the episode.
和这集内容完全无关。

1021
00:51:25.970 --> 00:51:27.230
Here's what it is.
事情是这样的。

1022
00:51:28.870 --> 00:51:33.670
Lady, you and I have been working really hard producing the podcast each week.
女士，你和我每周都在非常努力地制作播客。

1023
00:51:33.670 --> 00:51:37.850
We've been doing the final, final pass of our book.
我们一直在进行书稿的最终校对。

1024
00:51:38.010 --> 00:51:39.030
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1025
00:51:39.150 --> 00:51:39.930
The book.
那本书。

1026
00:51:40.110 --> 00:51:40.930
The book.
那本书。

1027
00:51:41.610 --> 00:51:43.710
We talk constantly.
我们一直在不停地交流。

1028
00:51:44.590 --> 00:51:47.310
But we talk about work.
但聊的都是工作。

1029
00:51:47.970 --> 00:51:52.290
We have not had a good BFF download in a few weeks.
我们已经好几周没有好好地进行闺蜜谈心了。

1030
00:51:52.290 --> 00:51:57.490
And to me, that feels like a very long time not to have a BFF download with you.
对我来说，没能和你进行闺蜜谈心，感觉已经过了好久好久。

1031
00:51:57.590 --> 00:51:57.890
I know.
我知道。

1032
00:51:58.070 --> 00:52:07.410
We used to at least once a week be able to grab lunch or breakfast or go for a walk or sit on one of our porches and just have just like a gal pal gab.
我们以前至少每周都能一起吃顿午饭或早饭，或者去散散步，或者坐在谁家的门廊上，像好姐妹一样闲聊。

1033
00:52:07.930 --> 00:52:15.630
I have three things that I have been wanting to talk to you about, but I've not had the chance because every time we're talking, it's about work.
我有三件事一直想跟你聊，但一直没机会，因为我们每次通话聊的都是工作。

1034
00:52:15.870 --> 00:52:17.150
Are we going to do it right here?
我们要现在就开始吗？

1035
00:52:17.390 --> 00:52:18.550
This is my moment.
这是我的时刻。

1036
00:52:18.790 --> 00:52:19.990
I need this moment.
我需要这个时刻。

1037
00:52:20.190 --> 00:52:20.570
Okay.
好吧。

1038
00:52:20.850 --> 00:52:26.990
And I'm just going to let everybody in on the types of things that I would bring up to you in a BFF download.
我要让大家听听，我会在闺蜜谈心中跟你聊些什么。

1039
00:52:27.770 --> 00:52:28.630
Are you ready?
你准备好了吗？

1040
00:52:28.790 --> 00:52:33.010
I wrote them on the card because I actually have been writing them down so I don't forget to tell you.
我把它们写在卡片上了，因为我真的把它们记下来了，免得忘了告诉你。

1041
00:52:33.190 --> 00:52:34.290
Yes, I'm so excited.
好，我太兴奋了。

1042
00:52:34.290 --> 00:52:35.830
I didn't see this coming today.
我没想到今天会有这一出。

1043
00:52:35.830 --> 00:52:37.910
I know, but this was my in.
我知道，但这可是我的切入点。

1044
00:52:38.270 --> 00:52:42.770
So the first one is something that has been bothering me for a really, really long time.
第一件事，是一件困扰我很久很久的事情。

1045
00:52:42.930 --> 00:52:44.910
And I have strong feelings about it.
而且我对此感触很深。

1046
00:52:45.070 --> 00:52:48.910
I need to get it off my chest and I don't want people to come for me.
我需要一吐为快，而且我不希望大家来攻击我。

1047
00:52:49.030 --> 00:52:49.450
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1048
00:52:49.630 --> 00:52:49.810
Okay?
好吗？

1049
00:52:50.210 --> 00:52:50.430
Okay.
好的。

1050
00:52:50.430 --> 00:52:52.670
But you're my BFF and I can say this to you.
但你是我的闺蜜，我可以跟你说这些。

1051
00:52:52.810 --> 00:52:53.150
Okay.
好吧。

1052
00:52:54.130 --> 00:52:56.270
What the f*** is up with sun butter?
向日葵黄油到底是什么鬼东西？

1053
00:52:56.670 --> 00:52:58.230
It is so gross.
太恶心了。

1054
00:52:58.230 --> 00:52:59.490
It tastes horrible.
味道糟透了。

1055
00:52:59.710 --> 00:53:00.990
Who is eating it?
到底是谁在吃啊？

1056
00:53:01.350 --> 00:53:03.390
Who is eating sunflower butter?
谁在吃向日葵黄油？

1057
00:53:04.150 --> 00:53:04.610
Who?
谁？

1058
00:53:04.610 --> 00:53:10.350
Oh, so this is the first I'm ever hearing of sun butter because, you know, I love just butter butter.
噢，这是我第一次听说向日葵黄油，因为你知道，我只爱普通的黄油。

1059
00:53:11.210 --> 00:53:13.890
No, sunflower butter is like...
不，向日葵黄油就像是……

1060
00:53:13.890 --> 00:53:14.290
Is it fakie butter?
是那种假黄油吗？

1061
00:53:14.570 --> 00:53:16.590
It's a peanut butter alternate.
它是花生酱的替代品。

1062
00:53:16.990 --> 00:53:17.330
Okay?
是吗？

1063
00:53:18.030 --> 00:53:26.490
You know, you've got almond butter, cashew butter, all these butters that are made out of tree nuts and nuts and seeds.
你知道的，有杏仁酱、腰果酱，所有这些用坚果和种子做的酱。

1064
00:53:26.490 --> 00:53:30.990
And they have made a spread out of sunflower seeds.
他们还用葵花籽做了一种抹酱。

1065
00:53:31.230 --> 00:53:32.490
And Angela, it's gross.
安吉拉，那真的很恶心。

1066
00:53:32.490 --> 00:53:33.910
It is not good.
一点都不好吃。

1067
00:53:34.110 --> 00:53:39.970
And I just need to know, is anyone, like, buying it for a second time?
我只想知道，有没有人会买第二次？

1068
00:53:40.170 --> 00:53:42.530
Because you'll buy it and be like, oh, sunflower butter.
因为你第一次买的时候可能会想，噢，向日葵黄油。

1069
00:53:42.690 --> 00:53:44.010
This might be really delicious.
这尝起来可能很美味。

1070
00:53:44.270 --> 00:53:45.630
Let me eat it.
让我尝尝。

1071
00:53:45.630 --> 00:53:48.630
But does anyone buy it for a second time?
但真的有人会回购吗？

1072
00:53:49.210 --> 00:53:49.650
Anyone?
有人吗？

1073
00:53:50.230 --> 00:53:52.510
Cassie, Sam, feel free to weigh in on this.
凯西，萨姆，你们尽管发表意见。

1074
00:53:52.650 --> 00:53:54.350
Your feelings on sunflower butter.
你们对向日葵黄油的看法。

1075
00:53:55.450 --> 00:53:57.210
I've never heard of sunflower butter.
我从没听说过向日葵黄油。

1076
00:53:57.330 --> 00:53:58.370
Thank you, Cassie.
谢谢你，凯西。

1077
00:53:58.470 --> 00:53:58.970
Thank you.
谢谢。

1078
00:53:59.050 --> 00:53:59.930
I have no idea this exists.
我完全不知道还有这东西。

1079
00:54:00.130 --> 00:54:00.890
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1080
00:54:01.110 --> 00:54:02.910
Three of us had never heard of it.
我们三个人都没听说过。

1081
00:54:03.110 --> 00:54:04.590
Guys, don't buy it.
伙计们，千万别买。

1082
00:54:04.910 --> 00:54:05.350
Okay?
好吗？

1083
00:54:05.350 --> 00:54:07.690
My God, the sun butter people are coming for you.
天哪，向日葵黄油厂商要来找你麻烦了。

1084
